{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "2f9fcb52-2257-4678-9f7f-4881ce2da740",
    "name": "e-commerce API · auth",
    "description": "The nine authentication endpoints of the e-commerce learning repo, served by `AuthController` at the `auth` root. These are the endpoints the two sibling collections do not cover: **e-commerce API (user context)** covers the five on `UserController`, **e-commerce API (product context)** the five on `ProductController`.\n\n**Before running:** start the API with `pnpm start:dev`, which brings up Postgres, Mongo and Mailpit through Docker Compose and boots Nest on the port in `.env` (3000 by default).\n\n**Variables:** everything shared (base URL, tokens, credentials, emailed tokens) lives in the **e-commerce (local)** environment rather than in collection variables, so all three collections read one session. Select that environment before running anything here or in the sibling collections; a collection pre-request guard aborts every request with a clear error when no environment is active, because the token writes would otherwise vanish silently.\n\n**Run order:** create the account first, with `Create user` in the user-context collection; it reads the same `{{userEmail}}` and `{{userPassword}}` from the environment, so the credentials match automatically. This collection deliberately does not duplicate `POST /users`, so that endpoint has one definition rather than two. Then run top to bottom: Resend verification, Verify email, Login, Refresh session, Change password, Logout, Logout all sessions, Forgot password, Reset password. Login and Refresh session store the tokens in the environment that every protected request in all three collections reads.\n\n**Two tokens never arrive over HTTP.** Verification and reset tokens are only ever emailed. Trigger the endpoint that sends the mail, then read the token out of Mailpit at http://localhost:8025 and paste it into `verificationToken` or `resetToken` in the environment.\n\n**Auth model:** `JwtAuthGuard` is registered as `APP_GUARD`, so every handler needs a bearer access token unless it carries `@Public()`. This collection sets bearer `{{accessToken}}` at the collection level and overrides the six public endpoints to No Auth. Authorization does not exist yet: any authenticated caller may act on any user (ADR 0015).\n\n**Status codes:** 400 comes from the validation pipe and carries no `code` field, while 422, 409, 404, 403 and 401 come from the typed exception filters and carry a stable `code`. A caller over a named throttle limit gets a 429 with no `code`. Four endpoints are throttled: login and reset-password at 10 per 60s, change-password at 10 per 60s, forgot-password and verify-email/resend at 5 per hour.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
