      "id": "b69cfa5d-439d-4863-ba05-cb85c43fc9d5",
      "description": "Each request here is named for the status it should produce. Several exist to document an *ordering* the happy paths cannot show: which check fires first when a request is wrong in two ways at once.",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Every request in this folder is named for the status it should",
              "// return, so one assertion here covers all of them and cannot drift",
              "// from the names the way eleven copies would.",
              "const expected = Number(pm.info.requestName.match(/^(\\d{3})/)[1]);",
              "",
              "pm.test(`${expected}`, () => pm.response.to.have.status(expected));",
              "",
              "// 400 comes from the validation pipe and carries no `code`; the typed",
              "// exception filters all do. 202 has no body at all.",
              "if (![202, 400].includes(expected)) {",
              "  pm.test('carries a stable code', () =>",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.be.a('string'));",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Resend verification",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('202', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "id": "67866b03-9538-46e5-9f77-7aa3febbca58",
      "request": {
        "auth": {
          "type": "noauth"
        },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-email/resend",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "auth",
            "verify-email",
            "resend"
          ]
        },
        "description": "202 whether or not the address exists, and 202 again if it is already verified with no mail sent. It cannot be used to probe for accounts.\n\nThrottled to 5 per hour: a hit spends someone else's inbox, not the caller's own resource. Read the token out of Mailpit and put it in `verificationToken`."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Verify email",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('204', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "id": "6d04c274-1fb3-4a11-82f3-8312ed0778e5",
      "request": {
        "auth": {
          "type": "noauth"
        },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"token\": \"{{verificationToken}}\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-email",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "auth",
            "verify-email"
          ]
        },
        "description": "204 on success.\n\nA POST carrying the token in the body, not a clickable GET. Link prefetchers, spam filters and corporate mail scanners follow links, and a GET that consumes a token gets consumed by a robot before the user clicks. The emailed link points at the frontend, which posts here.\n\nTTL comes from EMAIL_VERIFICATION_TTL_HOURS, 24h by default. An expired token answers 401 `AUTH_VERIFICATION_TOKEN_EXPIRED`, a spent or unknown one 401 `AUTH_VERIFICATION_TOKEN_INVALID`. Two codes rather than one is deliberate: the token reaches the account owner's inbox, so telling the holder \"expired, request another\" leaks nothing to anyone who does not already hold the link."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Login",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('returns a bearer session', () => {",
              "  const body = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(body.tokenType).to.eql('Bearer');",
              "  pm.expect(body.expiresIn).to.be.a('number');",
              "});",
              "",
              "// Written to the shared environment so every protected request in",
              "// all three collections reads the same session.",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  const body = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.environment.set('accessToken', body.accessToken);",
              "  pm.environment.set('refreshToken', body.refreshToken);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "id": "4562523d-38f7-4f50-8a29-017084c1e0ca",
      "request": {
        "auth": {
          "type": "noauth"
        },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "auth",
            "login"
          ]
        },
        "description": "200 with an access token, a refresh token, and the access token's TTL in seconds.\n\nA wrong password and an unknown address answer identically, 401 `AUTH_INVALID_CREDENTIALS`, so this endpoint is not an account-existence oracle. `POST /users` is one: it answers 409 on a duplicate email.\n\nAn unverified address answers 403 `AUTH_EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED`.\n\nThrottled to 10 per 60s. Every attempt spends 19 MiB in argon2 whether the password is right or not, so the limit pays for that cost decision rather than only guarding against brute force."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Refresh session",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "// The presented token is dead after this call, so overwriting is",
              "// mandatory, not a convenience.",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  const body = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.environment.set('accessToken', body.accessToken);",
              "  pm.environment.set('refreshToken', body.refreshToken);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "id": "fd082903-e40a-4df7-9b9f-2ea37dc8a2d8",
      "request": {
        "auth": {
          "type": "noauth"
        },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "auth",
            "refresh"
          ]
        },
        "description": "200 with a fresh access token and a **rotated** refresh token. Public: presenting the refresh token is the authentication.\n\nThe presented token is dead once this succeeds, so replaying one answers 401 `AUTH_REFRESH_TOKEN_INVALID` and the reuse also kills the chain. The test script overwrites `refreshToken`, so run this once per stored token.\n\nReplayed, expired, revoked and unknown all answer that one code, the opposite of the two-code split on the emailed tokens: a refresh token is held by whoever presents it rather than delivered to an inbox, so naming which check fired would tell an attacker that reuse detection triggered."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Change password",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('204', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));",
              "",
              "// Keeps Login runnable: the old password no longer exists.",
              "if (pm.response.code === 204) {",
              "  pm.environment.set('userPassword', pm.environment.get('newPassword'));",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "id": "5889a112-65b8-4387-b577-8608514858ac",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"currentPassword\": \"{{userPassword}}\",\n  \"newPassword\": \"{{newPassword}}\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/change-password",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "auth",
            "change-password"
          ]
        },
        "description": "204 on success. Protected, and the body still carries the current password: a valid access token proves the caller holds a token, not that they are the account owner. Requiring the current password is what stops a stolen access token turning into permanent account takeover inside its fifteen-minute window.\n\nRevokes every **other** session and spares this one, which is what a user expects from changing their own password rather than recovering it. Reset password does the opposite.\n\nA wrong `currentPassword` answers 401 `AUTH_INVALID_CREDENTIALS`. The new password's length is checked *before* that, so a new password outside 12 to 128 characters answers 422 `USER_PASSWORD_INVALID` even when the current password is wrong.\n\nThrottled to 10 per 60s, because the check is an argon2 verify against a caller-supplied guess: without a limit a stolen access token would buy an attacker one guess per request for the token's whole life."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Logout",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('204', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "id": "a2e5d124-6599-4a84-9743-ce1e17a14d57",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/logout",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "auth",
            "logout"
          ]
        },
        "description": "204, no body sent and none returned. The session comes from the access token's `sid` claim, so a client that has lost its refresh token can still end the session.\n\nEnds renewal, not access: the guard does no per-request revocation lookup, so `{{accessToken}}` keeps working until it expires. That is why Logout all sessions still succeeds after this one."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Logout all sessions",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('204', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "id": "fb8d1325-b849-4cec-92ae-f29fee8eaba2",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/logout-all",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "auth",
            "logout-all"
          ]
        },
        "description": "204. Revokes every refresh chain of the caller's user, including the one it was called from.\n\nSame caveat as Logout: renewal stops, existing access tokens keep working until they expire."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Forgot password",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('202', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "id": "a8b4ccfe-9b01-4dfb-be4f-1a2220d29832",
      "request": {
        "auth": {
          "type": "noauth"
        },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
