          "path": [
            "auth",
            "reset-password"
          ]
        },
        "description": "204 on success. Public: presenting the reset token is the authentication.\n\nRevokes **every** session including any the caller holds, because whoever prompted the reset may be holding one. Change password spares the current session; this deliberately does not.\n\nThe new password is validated and hashed *before* the token is touched, so a policy rejection does not cost the user their link. That ordering is observable: a short password with a garbage token answers 422 `USER_PASSWORD_INVALID`, not 401.\n\nOn the token itself, expired answers 401 `AUTH_RESET_TOKEN_EXPIRED` and spent or unknown 401 `AUTH_RESET_TOKEN_INVALID`.\n\nThrottled to 10 per 60s: because hashing happens first, a garbage token would otherwise buy a full argon2 hash for free every time."
      },
